        "created_at": "2014-12-11T08:49:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello folks,</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Firstly, if there is objection to me posting about another game that is currently on Kickstarter then please delete this thread, I'm not in any way related to this project just a keen backer of a game that I believe a lot of you would also get a kick out of, and a small publisher who I believe to genuinely deserve a bit of support, hence why I'm specifically posting here.</p><p><em>Too Many Cinderellas</em> is a Japanese micro game that the small Australian publisher Grail Games is bringing to the English language. It's a quick filler which also packs in enough game to keep it replayable (think micro games along the line of Council of Verona or Coup), and has a cute theme of the prince searching for his mysterious CInderella. It's also affordable at only £8.50/$13.00/e10.50 including worldwide shipping, and curently hanging at just a hundred backers short of hitting funding.</p><p>If you would like to know more then why not mosey on over to <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1986861668/too-many-cinderellas\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">their KS page</a> and maybe consider helping the project to hit funding.</p>",
